<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghaznavid Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ghaznavid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ghaznavid Empire was a Turkic Muslim dynasty based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazni">Ghazni</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, which ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a> and raided deep into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the late tenth and eleventh centuries. Its defeat by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dandanaqan">Battle of Dandanaqan</a> in 1040 opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> to the Seljuk Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghaznavid-empire.jpg" alt="Ghaznavid Empire" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Beylarbey · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghaznavids.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
